# Debian instrument and auxiliary server

Debian stable cloud image: Trixie 13, official build 20261116-2664.
Index URL: https://cdimage.debian.org/images/cloud/trixie/latest/
Dated image: https://cdimage.debian.org/images/cloud/trixie/20261116-2664/debian-13-generic-amd64-20261116-2664.qcow2
Published checksum: https://cdimage.debian.org/images/cloud/trixie/20261116-2664/SHA512SUMS
The official index timestamps the generic amd64 image 2026-11-16 17:46 UTC.
No detached signature is linked in that official build index. The downloaded
image matches the published SHA512 (`raw/debian/verification.log` and
`raw/debian/published-sha512.txt`).

`prepare.sh` downloads and verifies on the host, creates read-only cloud-image
backings and a NoCloud seed with user `user`, the laboratory key, and passwordless
sudo. `debian` has 4 GiB / 2 vCPU / 20 GiB; `debian-server` has 8 GiB / 4 vCPU /
40 GiB and takes two slot locks. Each disposable overlay performs cloud-init
on first boot. No package update is requested by the seed.

Cloud-init documentation: https://docs.cloud-init.io/en/latest/reference/datasources/nocloud.html
“NoCloud” provides configuration locally; user-data and meta-data are required.

`validate.py HOST_ALIAS` is the instrument validation driver. The caller supplies
the host alias; it is not part of published inputs. Expectations are recorded
before execution in `raw/runner-expectations.md`; the recorded assertions passed
in `raw/debian/runner-validation.json`, including explicit creation of both variants.
This validation was repeated after the runner changed to stream output without
buffering it in host memory. The stdin and lock timeout checks are separately
recorded in `raw/debian/timeout-supplement.json`. Disposable VMs were destroyed.
